quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  2,49,"(Remember) when We delivered you from Pharaoh’s people, who had oppressed you terribly, slaying your sons and sparing your daughters. There was a great trial in that from your Lord."
  2,50,"(Recall) When We parted the sea for you, We delivered you and drowned Pharaoh’s people as you were yourselves watching."
  2,51,"(Remember) when We settled with Musa (Moses) an appointment for forty nights. Then you took up the calf (for worship) in his absence, and you were transgressors."
  2,52,We still pardoned you after that; perhaps you would be thankful.
  2,53,"And (remember) when We gave Musa (Moses) the Book and the Criterion (that distinguishes between right and wrong), perhaps you might be guided."
  2,54,"And (recall) when Musa (Moses) said to his people: ‘Indeed you have wronged yourselves, my people, by taking up the calf (for worship). Now turn in repentance to your Creator. So, slay (the guilty among) your folks. This (act) would be better for you (as repentance) in the sight of your Creator.’ Then He relented towards you. Indeed, He is the Most-Clement, the All-Merciful."
  2,55,"(Remember) when you said: ‘O Musa (Moses)! We will not believe you until we see Allah manifestly.’ So, a thunderbolt struck you while you were watching."
  2,56,Then We revived you after your death (accepting Musa’s supplication) so that you might become thankful.
  2,57,"And (remember when) We shaded you with clouds (in the Tiha valley) and sent down to you manna and quails, saying: ‘Eat of the good things We have given you.’ They did not harm Us (by disobeying), but they used to harm (only) themselves."
